---
system: sys-01-identity-household-access
flow_id: session-revoke
surface: mobile
spec_anchor: /software/systems/01-identity-household-access#get-v1identitysessions
actors: [ParentApp, Gateway, IdentityService, PostgreSQL]
apis:
  - GET /v1/identity/sessions
  - DELETE /v1/identity/sessions/{jti}
externals: []
queues: []
failure_paths:
  - session_not_found
  - not_authorized
idempotency: revoke is idempotent on jti — repeated DELETE returns 200
retry: caller-side exponential backoff with jitter on 5xx — never retry on 4xx
timeout: 2s p99
status: final
---
%% HAND-CURATED.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant ParentApp
    participant Gateway
    participant IdentityService
    participant PostgreSQL

    Note over ParentApp,IdentityService: Entry point: parent_settings → Active Sessions — parent views + revokes other-device sessions

    ParentApp->>Gateway: GET /v1/identity/sessions
    Gateway->>Gateway: require valid parent JWT; extract user_id
    Gateway->>IdentityService: forward request
    IdentityService->>PostgreSQL: SELECT jti, device_name, platform, created_at, last_seen_at, ip_hash FROM parent_sessions WHERE user_id={user_id} AND revoked_at IS NULL ORDER BY last_seen_at DESC USING parent_sessions_active_by_user_idx
    PostgreSQL-->>IdentityService: sessions[]
    IdentityService-->>Gateway: 200 {sessions: [{jti, device_name, platform, created_at, last_seen_at, is_current}]}
    Gateway-->>ParentApp: 200 sessions list

    Note over ParentApp: parent selects a session to revoke (other device or current device)

    ParentApp->>Gateway: DELETE /v1/identity/sessions/{jti}
    Gateway->>Gateway: require valid parent JWT; extract caller_user_id + caller_jti
    Gateway->>IdentityService: forward request
    alt session_not_found (jti absent or already revoked — idempotent)
        IdentityService-->>Gateway: 200 already_revoked
        Gateway-->>ParentApp: 200
    else not_authorized (jti belongs to a different user_id)
        IdentityService-->>Gateway: 403 not_authorized
        Gateway-->>ParentApp: 403
    else revoke_success
        IdentityService->>PostgreSQL: UPDATE parent_sessions SET revoked_at=now() WHERE jti={jti} AND user_id={caller_user_id}
        PostgreSQL-->>IdentityService: updated
        IdentityService-->>Gateway: 200 {jti, revoked_at, self_revoke: (jti == caller_jti)}
        Gateway-->>ParentApp: 200
        alt self_revoke (parent revoked their own current session jti)
            ParentApp->>ParentApp: forced logout — clear auth.store + navigate to login screen
        else other_device_revoke
            ParentApp->>ParentApp: remove revoked session from list UI
        end
    end

    Note over ParentApp,IdentityService: timeout 2s p99 — hot kill via parent_sessions_active_by_user_idx (SM plan §8.4) — revoke idempotent on jti
